{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01FDFasPbdg69XFcaY353GoZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. I wrote and committed **Q8: Trim prompts + cache embeddings — before/after cost breakdown** (`answers/07-008-trim-prompts-cache-embeddings-beforeafter-cost-breakdown.md`).\n\n**Key content:**\n- **Two separate cost buckets** — generation (where the real dollars are) vs embedding (latency/rate-limit protection, modest dollar savings)\n- **Concrete before/after table** for a 500K queries/day RAG chatbot:\n  - Generation cost: **$6,300 → $1,400/day (~78% reduction)** via: cross-encoder rerank to top-3 chunks (5× context reduction), manual prompt audit, LLMLingua compression, `max_tokens` + conciseness instruction\n  - Embedding cost: **~40% reduction** via SHA-256 hash-match doc embedding cache (95% skip rate) + Redis query embedding cache (30% hit rate on FAQ traffic)\n- **Critical insight called out:** embedding cost is typically 5-10% of total spend — the dollar ROI is modest, but the latency and rate-limit benefits are material\n- **Quality gate discipline:** RAGAS Faithfulness ≥ 0.85 on 200-query golden dataset at each compression step\n- **3 specific pitfalls** covering: over-indexing on embedding cache savings, vague \"trim the prompt\" without naming buckets and percentages, and skipping quality validation\n\n9 items remaining in the Next queue (Q9–Q16 + validate)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":243,"cache_read_input_tokens":76704,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":243,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"063a0856-6083-49b3-87a2-bfadc151b91f","uuid":"b512644e-dd2c-4486-89cc-7e007ca5e888"}
